// A threshold is refused rather than approximated by the moving-wall law. In the
// steady kernel the dead branch is cheap because the asked drop is known and the
// bracket can stop at Q = 0 (5.46, 5.47); here the drop is what the row solves
// for, so static hold has to be integrated in time and needs a branch of its own.
// Refusing is what turns 5.45 - 5.47's documented boundary into an assertion.
// verified by tests/check_transient_power_law.py (family 5).
fluid { rho 850; mu 0.1; }
nodes { A { fixedPressure 3.0e4; } B { fixedPressure 2.0e4; } }
pipes { Bad { from A; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02; yieldStress 5.0; } }
time  { dt 0.02; endTime 0.1; reportEvery 1; }
